# Local override for the memQL binary's environment.
#
# Copy this file to .env in this same directory; the binary will
# layer your values on top of whatever the genesis envelope (or
# host shell) painted into the process environment. .env is
# gitignored, so each developer keeps their own copy.
#
# Authoritative source: memql/component/genesis/localenv.go.
#
# Rules:
#   - One KEY=VALUE per line. # for comments. Blank lines OK.
#   - Optional matching single/double quotes around the value.
#   - Optional `export ` prefix tolerated.
#   - MEMQL_MASTER_KEY is the one variable that CANNOT be
#     overridden here -- genesis owns it as the trust anchor.
#     Everything else is fair game.
#
# Typical entries (uncomment + edit what you need):

# Observability verbosity. Controls how much per-call detail the
# observe runtime captures. Off in production by default; turn it
# up locally to see args / results in the cockpit drill-down.
#   off     -- no per-call instrumentation
#   count   -- count + duration + error (cheap, always safe)
#   meta    -- + arg types + arg sizes (no values)
#   verbose -- + full arg / return values (subject to redaction)
# MEMQL_OBSERVE_LEVEL=verbose

# Override the embedded DSL tree with an on-disk one. Useful when
# you're hacking .memql files and don't want to rebuild the binary
# between every edit.
# MEMQL_DSL_PATH=/Users/me/projects/memql/dsl

# Switch the default SI provider without touching the manifest.
# MEMQL_DEFAULT_PROVIDER=chat54Mini

# Bump log verbosity locally.
# MEMQL_LOG_LEVEL=debug

# Identity access-token TTL. Defaults to 900 (15 min) in production.
# Drop to 180 (3 min) when you want to exercise the cockpit's silent
# refresh-token path quickly -- 15-min waits are tedious when you're
# trying to see whether refresh actually fires. The refresh-token TTL
# (IDENTITY_REFRESH_TOKEN_TTL_SECONDS, default 30 days) is independent
# of this and doesn't need to change.
# IDENTITY_ACCESS_TOKEN_TTL_SECONDS=180
